Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:34:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/27] kv-cache fp8: the KV8 device code compiles and its
 launch records register

stage_kv8_tile takes the KV-head count as an argument (HK is a runtime
parameter of attn_chunks, not file scope), its definition sits in
fn_attn with the decls that name it, the paged key_at table is back,
and fn_attn_prep_media_kv8 is defined (the glue loads it by symbol).
The four launches record their nvcc 13.3 resources for the five SMs.
